Exit with status 1 on an invalid * width or precision in printf.
get_width_prec() reported an invalid width or precision argument but
left the error in errno, and print_direc() clears errno before the
conversion, so the error never reached the exit status: "printf '%*d'
x 5" said "invalid number 'x'" and exited with status 0. Invalid
numbers in other arguments exit with status 1, as in bash and
coreutils.

Record the error in conv_err directly.

---
